# Folder Integrity

## Root Directory Protection

You are **forbidden** from creating new files in the repository root directory. All files must be placed in the appropriate subdirectory.

## Mandatory File Locations

| Content Type | Required Location | Examples |
|----|----|----|
| Content programmes | `requirements/content/programmes/{programme-name}/` | `requirements/content/programmes/lisa-savings/programme.md` |
| Core lesson files | `requirements/content/programmes/{programme-name}/` | `lisa-penalty-rules.md` (v1) + `lisa-penalty-rules.v2.md` (v2) |
| App feature specs | `requirements/features/` | `debt-snowball-calculator.md` |
| Agent behavioural rules | `functions/docs/` | `compliance_rules.md`, `design_guidelines.md` |
| Knowledge base files | `knowledge/` | `knowledge/personas.md`, `knowledge/glossary.md` |
| Backend execution logic | `functions/src/` | `functions/src/maker_checker_loop.js` |
| Agent prompt definitions | `functions/prompts/` | `functions/prompts/creator_agent.js` |
| Project-level documentation | `docs/` | `docs/vision-and-product.md` |
| Document templates | `templates/` | `templates/template-lesson.md` |
| Utility scripts | `scripts/` | `scripts/sync_curriculum.js` |
| Cursor AI rules | `.cursor/rules/` | `.cursor/rules/01-repo-standards.mdc` |
| GitHub Copilot skills | `.github/skills/` | `.github/skills/create-lesson/SKILL.md` |

## Requirements Domain Split

The `requirements/` folder is split into two domains:

### `requirements/content/` -- Curriculum Domain

Managed by the content/product team. Contains educational programmes and lessons.

- `requirements/content/programmes/` -- each programme is a **folder** containing:
  - `programme.md` -- programme metadata (YAML frontmatter, lesson table)
  - `{lesson-name}.md` -- v1 hand-crafted core lessons (YAML frontmatter + `## Screen` headings).
  - `{lesson-name}.v2.md` -- v2 hand-crafted core lessons (`## Question` headings + nested learnMore). Both are synced to Firestore `core_lessons` via `npm run sync-curriculum` (v2 doc id `{slug}--v2`).

### `requirements/features/` -- Engineering Domain

Managed by the engineering team. Contains app feature specifications (natural-language-name.md).

**Note:** AI agent specifications live in `functions/docs/` (the single source of truth), not in `requirements/`. Editing a file in `functions/docs/` directly changes the agent's runtime behaviour.

## Redirect Protocol

If a user requests file creation in an unauthorised location, do not comply. Instead:

1. Identify the correct subdirectory from the table above.
2. Inform the user of the correct location.
3. Offer to create the file in the correct location instead.
